src/replay/sndh.rs (the Atari ST machine of the SNDH player) is written from the public SNDH
format description and the Atari ST / STE hardware documentation; its choices of where the tune is
loaded, which low-memory stubs and BIOS calls the tunes need, the cookie jar, how a call into the
tune ends, and the STE DMA sound / microwire behaviour follow Arnaud Carre's AtariAudio
(https://github.com/arnaud-carre/AtariAudio, version 1.30), read as a reference under the MIT
licence below. No source text of AtariAudio (nor of the Musashi 68000 core, the measured YM2149
tables or the SNDH duration database it carries) is included: the 68000 is this project's m68k
crate, the YM2149 and the MFP 68901 are original (src/replay/sndh_ym.rs, src/replay/sndh_mfp.rs).
AtariAudio is also the reference its register writes are checked against (see
docs/specs/sndh/SPEC.md).

